# Step 23, the interactive application: its rules broken one at a time,
# with the tests that must fail. Written with the code.

[break] a-caught-panic-puts-the-terminal-back
rule: A panic on a thread other than the one that entered the terminal does not put the terminal back: the program may catch it and go on drawing.
file: crates/cortex-term/src/terminal.rs
in: restores_on_panic
find: == Some(std::thread::current().id())
replace: .is_some()
caught-by:
    cortex-term::it system::sys_a_panic_caught_on_another_thread_leaves_the_terminal_to_the_program

[break] no-panic-puts-the-terminal-back
rule: A panic on the thread that entered the terminal puts it back before the panic's message is printed.
file: crates/cortex-term/src/terminal.rs
in: restores_on_panic
find: == Some(std::thread::current().id())
replace: == None
caught-by:
    cortex-term::it system::sys_the_terminal_is_put_back_after_a_panic

[break] tui-settings-a-project-may-set
rule: Every key of [tui], [keys] and [terminal] is the user's own: a project's file cannot change how the user's terminal looks or which keys do what.
file: crates/cortex-config/src/schema/sections.rs
find:
    [UserOnly, Now]
    pub glyphs
replace:
    [Preference, Now]
    pub glyphs
caught-by:
    cortex-config::it trust::every_key_has_a_trust_class

[break] the-interface-cannot-hold-later-calls
rule: A core whose front end can stop the turn from a question holds every later call with side effects while the question is open.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/policy.rs
in: EnginePolicy::answers_may_stop
find: || self.stops_from_questions
replace:
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it approvals::with_answers_may_stop_a_later_call_waits_for_the_open_question

[break] the-wake-hook-every-event
rule: The queue's hook is called when it goes from empty to holding something, not for every event: one wake a burst.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/events.rs
in: EventQueue::queued
find: if was_empty {
replace: if true {
caught-by:
    events::tests::the_wake_hook_is_called_once_a_burst_and_when_the_queue_closes

[break] the-wake-hook-never-on-close
rule: Closing a client's queue calls its hook, so a reader on its own thread learns the client is gone.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/events.rs
in: EventQueue::close
find:
    self.wake.notify_one();
    let hook = lock(&self.hook).clone();
replace:
    self.wake.notify_one();
    let hook: Option<Wake> = None;
caught-by:
    events::tests::the_wake_hook_is_called_once_a_burst_and_when_the_queue_closes

[break] a-dialog-takes-typing-meant-for-the-editor
rule: A dialog drawn while the person is typing takes keys only from a grace after its first frame: keys typed before they could see it are the editor's.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/dialog.rs
in: Dialog::takes_keys_at
find: (!self.typing || at >= shown + GRACE)
replace: true
caught-by:
    app::tests::a_dialog_that_appears_while_the_person_types_takes_keys_only_after_a_grace

[break] a-dialog-answered-before-it-is-drawn
rule: A key read before a dialog's first frame was written never answers it.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/dialog.rs
in: Dialog::takes_keys_at
find: at >= shown &&
replace:
caught-by:
    app::tests::a_dialog_that_appears_while_the_person_types_takes_keys_only_after_a_grace

[break] no-second-interrupt
rule: A second interrupt within two seconds of the first stops running commands at once.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::interrupt
find: at.saturating_duration_since(last) <= SECOND_INTERRUPT
replace: false
caught-by:
    app::tests::esc_right_after_enter_interrupts_and_a_second_within_two_seconds_stops_now

[break] running-only-once-the-turn-starts
rule: A prompt sent makes the interface running at once, so that Esc straight after Enter interrupts the turn it started.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::submit
find:
    if started {
        self.start_running(at);
    }
replace:
caught-by:
    app::tests::esc_right_after_enter_interrupts_and_a_second_within_two_seconds_stops_now

[break] events-not-held-while-opening
rule: The session's events are held while the app's open is under way, so that its header is the first block.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::drain
find: if self.opening {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    app::tests::the_session_is_opened_after_the_first_frame_and_its_header_comes_first
